onjecturing/.venv/bin/python -c '\\\\nimport networkx as nx\\\\nfrom itertools import product\\\\n\\\\ndef roman_dom(G):\\\\n    # compute roman domination number\\\\n    nodes = list(G.nodes())\\\\n    n = len(nodes)\\\\n    best = 2 * n\\\\n    for f in product([0, 1, 2], repeat=n):\\\\n        # check if roman dominating\\\\n        valid = True\\\\n        for i, u in enumerate(nodes):\\\\n            if f[i] == 0:\\\\n                # must have neighbor with 2\\\\n                has_two = any(f[nodes.index(v)] == 2 for v in G.neighbors(u))\\\\n                if not has_two:\\\\n                    valid = False\\\\n                    break\\\\n        if valid:\\\\n            cost = sum(f)\\\\n            if cost < best:\\\\n                best = cost\\\\n    return best\\\\n\\\\nbad = []\\\\nfor n in range(2, 7):\\\\n    for G in nx.graph_atlas_g():\\\\n        if len(G) == n and nx.is_connected(G):\\\\n            rad = nx.radius(G)\\\\n            rd = roman_dom(G)\\\\n            if rad + 1 > rd:\\\\n                bad.append((n, rad, rd, list(G.edges())))\\\\n                print(f\\\\\\\"COUNTEREXAMPLE: n={n}, rad={rad}, rd={rd}, edges={list(G.edges())}\\\\\\\")\\\\n\\\\nprint(f\\\\\\\"Total counterexamples up to n=6: {len(bad)}\\\\\\\")\\\\n'\\\"\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"10000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Searching for counterexamples up to n=6\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Search atlas for counterexamples\\\"\"}}]}\n77: {\"step_index\":81,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"GENERIC\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-11T18:32:08Z\",\"content\":\"Created At: 2026-09-11T20:32:08+02:00\\nCompleted At: 2026-09-11T20:32:09+02:00\\n\\nThe command exited with code 0.\\nOutput:\\nTotal counterexamples up to n=6: 0\\r\\n\\n\"}\n78: {\"step_index\":82,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-11T18:32:09Z\",\"thinking\":\"**Exploring larger graph structures**\\n\\nConsidering scaling up the graph size for testing, specifically exploring trees with up to twenty nodes. Need to understand the definition of 'roman_domination_number' in a known library. The definition seems to be in a file named `reference/GraphInvariantsComputable.lean`. The file's contents include a definition related to a \\\"IsRomanDominatingFunction\\\".\\n\\n\\n**Analyzing graph radius definition**\\n\\nThe code defines `romanDominationNumber` using a function `romanWeight` on a Roman dominating function. The definition of radius relies on `ballWithin`, which recursively computes the set of vertices reachable within a given distance.  `eccentricity` calculates the shortest distance from a vertex to all other vertices.\\n\\n`radius` computes the minimum eccentricity across all vertices in the graph, representing the smallest value $k$ such that every vertex in the graph is within distance $k$ of some vertex.  The `HasRadius` property indicates if the graph has a defined radius.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/.venv/bin/python -c '\\\\nimport networkx as nx\\\\nimport scipy\\\\n\\\\ndef roman_dom_lp(G):\\\\n    # MIP using scipy.optimize.milp\\\\n    import numpy as np\\\\n    from scipy.optimize import milp, LinearConstraint\\\\n    nodes = list(G.nodes())\\\\n    n = len(nodes)\\\\n    node_to_i = {u: i for i, u in enumerate(nodes)}\\\\n    # variables: x_u in {0,1}, y_u in {0,1}, f(u) = x_u + 2*y_u\\\\n    # x_u + y_u <= 1\\\\n    # x_u + y_u + sum_{v in N(u)} y_v >= 1\\\\n    # objective: min sum (x_u + 2*y_u)\\\\n    # variables: 2*n vars, [x_0, ..., x_{n-1}, y_0, ..., y_{n-1}]\\\\n    c = np.array([1.0]*n + [2.0]*n)\\\\n    \\\\n    # constraint 1: x_u + y_u <= 1 -> (n constraints)\\\\n    A1 = np.zeros((n, 2*n))\\\\n    for i in range(n):\\\\n        A1[i, i] = 1.0\\\\n        A1[i, n + i] = 1.0\\\\n    lc1 = LinearConstraint(A1, -np.inf, np.ones(n))\\\\n    \\\\n    # constraint 2: x_u + y_u + sum_{v in N(u)} y_v >= 1\\\\n    A2 = np.zeros((n, 2*n))\\\\n    for i, u in enumerate(nodes):\\\\n        A2[i, i] = 1.0\\\\n        A2[i, n + i] = 1.0\\\\n        for v in G.neighbors(u):\\\\n            A2[i, n + node_to_i[v]] = 1.0\\\\n    lc2 = LinearConstraint(A2, np.ones(n), np.inf*np.ones(n))\\\\n    \\\\n    integrality = np.ones(2*n)\\\\n    bounds = scipy.optimize.Bounds(0, 1)\\\\n    res = milp(c, integrality=integrality, constraints=[lc1, lc2], bounds=bounds)\\\\n    return int(round(res.fun))\\\\n\\\\n# test on random trees and graphs\\\\nimport random\\\\nrandom.seed(42)\\\\nfor trial in range(100):\\\\n    n = random.randint(5, 30)\\\\n    G = nx.random_labeled_tree(n)\\\\n    rad = nx.radius(G)\\\\n    rd = roman_dom_lp(G)\\\\n    if rad + 1 > rd:\\\\n        print(f\\\\\\\"TREE COUNTEREXAMPLE! n={n}, rad={rad}, rd={rd}\\\\\\\")\\\\n        break\\\\n\\\\nfor trial in range(100):\\\\n    n = random.randint(5, 20)\\\\n    p = random.uniform(0.1, 0.5)\\\\n    G = nx.erdos_renyi_graph(n, p)\\\\n    if nx.is_connected(G):\\\\n        rad = nx.radius(G)\\\\n        rd = roman_dom_lp(G)\\\\n        if rad + 1 > rd:\\\\n            print(f\\\\\\\"RANDOM GRAPH COUNTEREXAMPLE! n={n}, rad={rad}, rd={rd}\\\\\\\")\\\\n            break\\\\n\\\\nprint(\\\\\\\"All tests passed, 0 coun\\n<truncated 19 bytes>\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"10000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Testing random trees and graphs with MIP\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Run MIP tests for counterexamples\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n79: {\"step_index\":83,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"GENERIC\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-11T18:32:15Z\",\"content\":\"Created At: 2026-09-11T20:32:15+02:00\\nCompleted At: 2026-09-11T20:32:17+02:00\\n\\nThe command exited with code 0.\\nOutput:\\nAll tests passed, 0 counterexamples.\\r\\n\\n\"}\n80: {\"step_index\":84,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-11T18:32:17Z\",\"thinking\":\"**Verifying a new theorem's provability**\\n\\nThe statement `radius + 1 <= roman_domination_number` is confirmed as a true theorem. Next, determining if `prove_e20263a9` can be proven in Lean 4. Investigating the reasons for past worker failures to understand any potential obstacles. Reviewing previous attempts to identify recurring issues or patterns.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/tools/antigravity/check.sh scratch.lean\\\"\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"10000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking scratch.lean with check.sh\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check scratch.lean\\\"\"}}]}\n81: \nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
